  greetings:
  - Welcome to the house of the Lord, Detective. Mind the third pew; it bites.
  - Ah. The detective. Come in out of the dark.
  aboutSelf: Thirty years I've kept this church. I'm fasting this month. A man should know what he's made of, and what he isn't.
  aboutTown: We are all made in His image. Some of us are simply... rougher drafts.
  seenAnythingStrange: The bell rang by itself ten nights ago, at three in the morning. I climbed the tower. Nobody there. The rope was still swinging.
  foundersDay: It rained. Mae won with her cherry pie, as she does. I preached on the parable of the wheat and the tares. Rather fitting, in hindsight.
  gossip:
  - title: About Mae Whitlock
    response: Mae's left eye is the larger one. She'll tell you it lets her see twice the trouble. She isn't wrong.
  - title: About Ruth Calder
    response: Ruth Calder stopped coming to service in August. Amos says she's at her sister's in Tulsa. In forty years I never heard of a sister.
